WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:11.900
[Eagle Pictures presents Enemy X, Copyright
MCMXLII by Eagle Pictures, Inc.]

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.900
[The Players, Keith Prescott...William Harrigan,
Rollins Darwin...Edmond Dorsay, Dr. Crandall...Frederic

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:24.900
Tozere, Inspector Thorndyke...Royal Beal,
Tom Dudley...Robert Allen]

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.900
[Director of Photography....George Webber,
Art Director....Oscar Yerg, Film Editor....Shirley

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.500
Stone, Sound....Harold Vivian

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:39.100
[Written and Directed by Owen Murphy]

00:00:40.000 --> 00:01:12.000
[Piano music]

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:16.030
[Rawlins:] For heaven's sake, Keith, stop
that infernal racket and tell me what's up.

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:22.640
It must be something extraordinary to provoke
you to such musical lengths.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:28.939
[Keith:] This infernal racket as you so delicately
put it, Rawlins, happens to be one of Schumann's

00:01:28.939 --> 00:01:35.939
famous melodies. I think I play it rather
well, and something important has turned up.

00:01:39.509 --> 00:01:45.950
[Rawlins:] I knew it. That falderal at the
piano only confirmed my suspicions. What is

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:47.939
it this time? Something exciting?

00:01:47.939 --> 00:01:51.689
[Keith:] One of the most incredible cases
I've ever been called in on.

00:01:51.689 --> 00:01:54.350
[Rawlins:] Good. Good. Mystery I hope?

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:59.490
[Keith:] Mystery it is and unbelievable.

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:06.490
[Rawlins:] Wonderful. Wonderful. Unbelievable
mystery. Well, come on. Let's have it.

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:13.240
[Keith:] I received a message from Inspector
Thorndyke yesterday and I dropped in to see

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:20.240
him. The inspector seemed a little bit upset.
He had every reason to be as I learned later.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:23.440
Well, what's up, inspector?

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:26.690
[Inspector:] Plenty. I'm going nuts.

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:31.750
[Keith:] The inevitable ending to one in our
profession. What is speeding the day?

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:35.040
[Inspector:] Well, I suppose you read the
death of Senator Bentley yesterday?

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:40.420
[Keith:] Yes, I did. A great loss to the nation.
Bentley had more common sense than any man

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:46.800
in Congress. You know, we're going to miss
him. Very sudden wasn't it?

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:53.530
[Inspector:] Very. I hadn't the least bit
of evidence but I believe Bentley was murdered.

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:55.820
[Keith:] On what do you base your belief?

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:58.170
[Inspector:] There was the imprint of an X
on his forehead.

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:00.700
[Keith:] And you infer that was the signature
of the murderer?

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:05.200
[Inspector:] I know it is. Keith, one of the
greatest killers in the world is loose in

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:11.400
New York; 15 men and women found dead yesterday
and on the forehead of every one of them there

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.790
was scrawled an X.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:15.520
[Keith:] And yet no evidence of murder?

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:22.520
[Inspector:] None. [Telephone ringing] Yes?
Yes? 217 Center. I'll be right over. They

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:27.530
just got Major Cullens of the Interceptor
command.

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:28.610
[Keith:] Jim Cullens?

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:29.290
[Inspector:] Yeah.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:32.460
[Keith:] Why, he and I had lunch together
at the club yesterday.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:35.480
[Inspector:] Enemy X is killing the kind of
people we can't afford to lose.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:42.480
[ Background music. The two men enter a room
and see a man collapsed at his desk with his

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:55.650
head down. They lift his head up and see an
X on his forehead. ]

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:11.120
[Keith:] Jim was quite dead. Stricken by some
unseen enemy.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.530
[Rawlins:] But I say things like this just
don't happen.

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:20.289
[Keith:] Unfortunately, Rawlins, they are
happening and in every part of this nation.

00:04:20.289 --> 00:04:27.289
Over 400 people fell victims to Enemy X yesterday.
There were 400 died the day before. There

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:33.420
will be 400 today; 400 tomorrow.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:36.940
[Rawlins:] But that's unbelievable.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:43.940
[Keith:] It's the bitter truth. At this rate
155,000 men and women of the United States

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:53.950
are doomed by Enemy X to die this year. Men
and women of all walks of life; the poor,

00:04:54.840 --> 00:05:01.840
the rich, the famous, the unknown. Even you,
Rawlins, may be on the list. So may I.

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:08.400
[Rawlins:] But what can we do? What can we
do?

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:15.400
[Mr. Dudley:] Cut! All right, 10 minutes,
Frankie. [Save the lights? Save them?]. Ten

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:24.060
minutes everybody. Gentlemen, I'd like you
to meet Dr. Crandall; one of New York's most

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:25.230
eminent surgeons. Dr. Crandall, Mr. Dorsay.

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:25.830
[Dr. Crandall:] How do you do?

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:27.380
[Mr. Dudley:] Mr. Dorsay and Mr. Harrigan.

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:28.240
[Dr. Crandall:] Mr. Harrigan.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:29.570
[Mr. Harrigan:] How do you do, doctor.

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:33.110
[Dr. Crandall:] I enjoyed your scenes in the
proposed motion picture. It should be very

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:33.360
convincing.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:37.150
[Mr. Harrigan:] Well, I only hope it gives
the same jolt to our audience that it gave

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:42.840
to me. You know, doctor, I find it hard to
believe that 400 of our people die every day

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:43.230
of cancer.

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:47.880
[Dr. Crandall:] Well, the tragedy of it is,
Mr. Harrigan, that so many of these people

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:53.320
died needlessly. If the disease were discovered
in time, they could be cured.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:55.990
[Mr. Dorsay:] You mean if they go to their
doctor in time?

00:05:55.990 --> 00:05:59.990
[Dr. Crandall:] I mean they should go to a
competent physician at least once a year and

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:04.220
have a complete physical examination. In no
other way can this danger be averted.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:09.500
[Mr. Dudley:] Of course victims of cancer
are not stricken suddenly as our mystery picture

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:10.040
might indicate.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:14.250
[Dr. Crandall:] Oh, no, Mr. Dudley, I'm quite
sure that everyone knows that cancer is a

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:19.060
long and drawn-out disease. The technique
used in the picture is what one might term,

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:25.290
well, a theatrical license to emphasize our
point as is also the sinister sign of the

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:32.290
X. Each serves to illustrate the treachery
of this public enemy known as cancer.

00:06:32.699 --> 00:06:38.770
There the allegory ends and make no mistake
about the point of the lesson. Just as surely

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:45.770
as if they were slain by an unseen enemy 155,000
of our people will be killed by cancer this

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:46.680
year.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:50.389
[Mr. Dudley:] If it's as you say, doctor,
many of these could be saved it seems to me

00:06:50.389 --> 00:06:52.550
our job is to awaken them to the danger.

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:57.480
[Dr. Crandall:] You're exactly right, Mr.
Dudley. This is a struggle of life and death

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:04.139
and we cannot win if we're afraid or if we're
ignorant of our enemy's method of attack.

00:07:04.139 --> 00:07:09.150
Neither can we win by complacency. We've got
to jolt the people into action.

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:14.310
[Mr. Harrigan:] You mention fear, Dr. Crandall,
you mean that men and women are afraid to

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:15.320
go for an examination?

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:19.160
[Dr. Crandall:] I wish I could tell you of
the hundreds of instances that have come to

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:24.889
my attention, men and women who came to see
me but came too late because they were afraid,

00:07:24.889 --> 00:07:31.460
or as in the case of so many women a sense
of false modesty kept them away. They make

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:34.120
false modesty an ally of death.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:40.430
[Mr. Dorsay:] Let me get this straight, doctor.
If a man and woman feels in good health, should

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:41.710
they still have a physical examination?

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:46.400
[Dr. Crandall:] Well, it's precisely those
people we want to reach. Until certain symptoms

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:53.400
appear no one is aware that cancer has begun.
To be certain -- and remember, this is your

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:58.840
life -- you must have a complete physical
examination once a year.

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:03.389
[Mr. Harrigan:] There are so many questions
I would like to ask, doctor. Questions I'm

00:08:03.389 --> 00:08:06.860
sure that everybody would like to ask if they
had the opportunity.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:11.889
[Dr. Crandall:] Well, we wish everyone would
ask questions, Mr. Harrigan. Cancer is not

00:08:11.889 --> 00:08:18.889
something to be spoken of in whispers. There
should be open debate, public discussions,

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:23.110
such as recently took place on one of our
major networks.

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:29.800
[Mr. Bryson:] It's very important that these
serious diseases should be brought out in

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:34.320
the open. In fact, we ought to talk about
things like cancer, we ought to talk about

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:38.709
it, we ought to organize knowledge about it.
It's important that it be talked about. It's

00:08:38.709 --> 00:08:40.190
necessary for the state of the nation.

00:08:40.190 --> 00:08:45.519
[Dr. Little:] You're quite right, Mr. Bryson.
Everything concerning cancer should have the

00:08:45.519 --> 00:08:52.519
widest possible publicity, because only in
that way can the citizens of all the Americas

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:57.080
obtain the knowledge necessary to fight this
enemy.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:09:02.200
[Mr. Bryson:] You're in a position to know,
Dr. Little, if you're managing director of

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:06.600
the American Society for the Control of Cancer.
Is there real progress being made?

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:12.580
[Dr. Little:] Very definitely Mr. Bryson.
The people of the United States and the Latin

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:19.580
Americas are coming to be more and more interested
in the problem of cancer control. They realize

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:28.020
that cancer isn't a hopeless disease but that
it's curable and, in fact, is being cured

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:30.300
when discovered and treated in time.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:32.440
[Dr. Binkley:] If I might add to that.

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:33.990
[Mr. Bryson:] Yes, Dr. Binkley.

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:40.250
[Dr. Binkley:] And equally encouraging factor
in our fight to control cancer is whereas

00:09:40.250 --> 00:09:47.250
10 years ago we had only a few clinics serving
our people, today there are nearly 400 qualified

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:57.390
clinics serving our people. The research laboratories
have kept pace, added to which is the really

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:01.940
magnificent work of the Women's Field Army.

00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:06.000
[Mr. Bryson:] The Women's Field Army sounds
like a fine enterprise, Mrs. [Ellig?], you're

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.110
national commander of it. Can you tell us
something about it?

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:15.320
[Mrs. Ellig?]:] The Women's Field Army, Mr.
Bryson, is a voluntary group banded together

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:22.320
to fight cancer. Each of our 200,000 members,
and we wish that we might make it a million,

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:29.820
pays a dollar a year as a membership fee and
pledges to work for the control of cancer.

00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:35.950
[Mr. Bryson:] Mrs. [Ellig?], you've got 200,000
women enrolled for a fight for cancer control.

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:37.459
What is it that these women really do?

00:10:37.459 --> 00:10:44.330
[Mrs. [Ellig?]:] Within the limitations of
our funds, which are highly adequate for the

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:50.130
purpose, we endeavor to keep the message of
cancer control constantly before our respective

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:57.130
communities. This we do by serving as an information
center, by seeing to it that no one is without

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:05.560
proper medical treatment, and by ever lastingly
pounding away at the necessity of everyone

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:10.399
having a complete physical examination yearly.

00:11:10.399 --> 00:11:14.790
[Mr. Bryson:] Mrs. [Ellig?], I hope that in
every community where your Army is not already

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:19.920
established some public-spirited women can
be found who will do there what's being so

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:25.250
splendidly done where you are underway. This
has been very interesting and, of course,

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:31.450
it's much more than interesting; it's extremely
important. I'm sure that everyone feels that

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:36.430
it's an encouragement to know that we have
the scientific ways now of controlling cancer

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:40.480
and we know how to enlist the interest of
everyone.

00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:46.220
[Mr. Harrigan:] There are so many questions
come to mind, Dr. Crandall, but first and

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:49.990
most important what are the symptoms? How
will we know?

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:54.610
[Dr. Crandall:] There are certain indications,
Mr. Harrigan, that we must lock in our mind

00:11:54.610 --> 00:12:00.490
and forever remember. If you have a persistent
lump or thickening, especially the breast,

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:06.240
see your doctor at once. Watch for any irregular
bleeding or discharge from any of the body

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:13.240
openings. A sore that does not heal especially
about the mouth or lips or tongue is a danger

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:14.800
signal.

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:21.800
Look out for any sudden changes in the form
or rate of a mole or wart. And finally, be

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:31.850
wary of persistent indigestion especially
when accompanied by loss of weight. However,

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:38.850
I must emphasize that these symptoms are not
positive proof of cancer, but don't decide

00:12:39.459 --> 00:12:43.790
that for yourself. You must be guided by your
physician.

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:49.910
[Mr. Dorsay:] Thank you, Dr. Crandall. I feel
better about this now that I have a little

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:52.110
knowledge of what to expect and what to do.

00:12:52.110 --> 00:12:56.860
[Dr. Crandall:] And everyone will feel better,
Mr. Dorsay, once the fear of cancer is removed

00:12:56.860 --> 00:12:59.440
and the whole program is brought out into
the light of understanding.

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:03.500
[Mr. Harrigan:] I want to thank you too, doctor,
and I hope our little contribution helps in

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:03.940
the fight.

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:07.190
[Dr. Crandall:] Well, I'm sure it will, Mr.
Harrigan. This is a fight in which we must

00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:14.190
all engage. This is war and we must face the
enemy with courage. We are making progress.

00:13:14.279 --> 00:13:20.550
We are saving lives that might have been lost.
We have every reason to face the future with

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:22.920
cheer and hope and confidence.

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:28.900
[Mr. Dudley:] Hit the lights! Stand by everybody, for the scene.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:31.000
[Background music and conversations]

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:46.900
[Background music and conversations]

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:56.000
[People walking across a field]

00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:07.000
[Sign reading Fight cancer with knowledge]

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:13.000
[The End, An Eagle Production]

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:17.000
[This film has been produced under the joint
auspices of the American Society for the Control

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.000
of Cancer and the United States Public Health
Service. Grateful acknowledgement is tendered

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:32.000
to Mr. Lyman Bryson of the Columbia Broadcasting
System for his aid and participation.]

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:37.000
[Seal of the U. S. Public Health Service.
1798]

